{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your assistant forgets everything the moment a session ends. A user tells it their name\nthis week; next week it asks again. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" fixes that. It gives a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":"\nrun memory that survives across turns and across sessions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It works in two moves. Before the model runs, it "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"recalls"}]},{"type":"text","value":" relevant memory from a\npluggable adapter and adds it to the system prompt. After the run finishes, it "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"saves"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nthe turn. The save is deferred, so it never blocks streaming."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reach for it when you need recall across turns or sessions. To keep the last few messages\nof the same request, just pass them in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":". Memory is overkill for that."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Everything lives in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-memory"},{"type":"text","value":": the middleware, the adapter contract, and the\nbuilt-in and vendor adapters."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Want a copy-paste setup? See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./quickstart","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quickstart"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Building an adapter for a\nbackend that isn't shipped? See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./custom-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" guide."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-to-reach-for-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When to reach for it"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Need"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"Remember what the user told me last week\""}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory middleware with a persistent adapter"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"Each user has their own context\""}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory middleware with a scoped adapter"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"Use a hosted memory service (mem0, Honcho, Hindsight)\""}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The matching vendor adapter"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep the last few turns in the same request"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass them in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":", skip memory"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-contract-recall-and-save","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The contract: recall and save"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A memory adapter has one identifier and two verbs. Extraction, ranking, rendering, and\nstorage are all the adapter's job. The middleware never looks inside a record."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Member"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable identifier used in logs and devtools."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall(scope, query)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return what's relevant to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query"},{"type":"text","value":" within "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scope"},{"type":"text","value":": a rendered "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"systemPrompt"},{"type":"text","value":", optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fragments"},{"type":"text","value":", and optional LLM "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolGuidance"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save(scope, turn)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persist a finished "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ user, assistant }"},{"type":"text","value":" turn. Extraction happens here. Returns one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SaveReceipt"},{"type":"text","value":" per write."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inspect(scope)?"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional. A full snapshot for a devtools panel."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listFacts(scope)?"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional. A flat fact list for a devtools panel."}]}]]},{"type":"code","value":"// The MemoryAdapter contract, from `@tanstack/ai-memory`:\nimport type { MemoryAdapter } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in adapters, each a tree-shakeable subpath:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\nimport { redis } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/redis'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vendor adapters:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { hindsight } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/hindsight'\nimport { mem0 } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/mem0'\nimport { honcho } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/honcho'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapters"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for every adapter and its options."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-a-turn-flows","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How a turn flows"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recall"}]},{"type":"text","value":" runs before the model, during the run's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"init"},{"type":"text","value":" phase.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter.recall(scope, userText)"},{"type":"text","value":" returns memory, and the middleware adds the\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"systemPrompt"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolGuidance"},{"type":"text","value":", and any "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" to the run."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Save"}]},{"type":"text","value":" runs after the stream finishes, deferred through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.defer"},{"type":"text","value":" so it never\nblocks the response. The middleware hands the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ user, assistant }"},{"type":"text","value":" turn to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter.save(scope, turn)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To add telemetry, watch memory in devtools, persist without recalling, or handle\nfailures, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./operating","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Operating memory"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"scope-and-security","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scope and security"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MemoryScope"},{"type":"text","value":" is the isolation boundary. It is an alias of the shared "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Scope"},{"type":"text","value":" identity\ntype from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":" — the same vocabulary used by persistence — so memory and chat\ncenter on one conversation key:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// MemoryScope is an alias of Scope from `@tanstack/ai`, exported by `@tanstack/ai-memory`:\ntype MemoryScope = {\n  threadId: string // required — same as ChatMiddlewareContext.threadId\n  userId?: string\n  tenantId?: string\n  namespace?: string // reserved — no adapter keys on it yet\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Always resolve scope on the server from trusted session/auth state. A client-originated\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":" is fine only after you validate it belongs to the session user; never accept\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"userId"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tenantId"},{"type":"text","value":" from the request body alone. The function form of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scope"},{"type":"text","value":" runs per\nrequest and only sees what your server attached to the chat context:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport type { MemoryAdapter } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\n\ndeclare const adapter: MemoryAdapter\ndeclare function getSession(ctx: unknown): { threadId: string; userId: string }\n\nmemoryMiddleware({\n  adapter,\n  scope: (ctx) => {\n    const session = getSession(ctx) // your server-validated session\n    return { threadId: session.threadId, userId: session.userId }\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./quickstart","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quickstart"}]},{"type":"text","value":": wire "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" into a real "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapters"}]},{"type":"text","value":": every adapter's options, with an example of each"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./custom-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":": implement "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" for a backend that isn't shipped"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./operating","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Operating memory"}]},{"type":"text","value":": options, telemetry, devtools events, and failure behavior"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"when-to-reach-for-it","text":"When to reach for it","level":2},{"id":"the-contract-recall-and-save","text":"The contract: recall and save","level":2},{"id":"how-a-turn-flows","text":"How a turn flows","level":2},{"id":"scope-and-security","text":"Scope and security","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYour assistant forgets everything the moment a session ends. A user tells it their name\nthis week; next week it asks again. `memoryMiddleware` fixes that. It gives a `chat()`\nrun memory that survives across turns and across sessions.\n\nIt works in two moves. Before the model runs, it **recalls** relevant memory from a\npluggable adapter and adds it to the system prompt. After the run finishes, it **saves**\nthe turn. The save is deferred, so it never blocks streaming.\n\nReach for it when you need recall across turns or sessions. To keep the last few messages\nof the same request, just pass them in `messages`. Memory is overkill for that.\n\nEverything lives in `@tanstack/ai-memory`: the middleware, the adapter contract, and the\nbuilt-in and vendor adapters.\n\n> Want a copy-paste setup? See the [Quickstart](./quickstart). Building an adapter for a\n> backend that isn't shipped? See the [Custom Adapter](./custom-adapter) guide.\n\n## When to reach for it\n\n| Need | Use this |\n|------|----------|\n| \"Remember what the user told me last week\" | Memory middleware with a persistent adapter |\n| \"Each user has their own context\" | Memory middleware with a scoped adapter |\n| \"Use a hosted memory service (mem0, Honcho, Hindsight)\" | The matching vendor adapter |\n| Keep the last few turns in the same request | Pass them in `messages`, skip memory |\n\n## The contract: recall and save\n\nA memory adapter has one identifier and two verbs. Extraction, ranking, rendering, and\nstorage are all the adapter's job. The middleware never looks inside a record.\n\n| Member | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `id` | Stable identifier used in logs and devtools. |\n| `recall(scope, query)` | Return what's relevant to `query` within `scope`: a rendered `systemPrompt`, optional `fragments`, and optional LLM `tools` plus `toolGuidance`. |\n| `save(scope, turn)` | Persist a finished `{ user, assistant }` turn. Extraction happens here. Returns one `SaveReceipt` per write. |\n| `inspect(scope)?` | Optional. A full snapshot for a devtools panel. |\n| `listFacts(scope)?` | Optional. A flat fact list for a devtools panel. |\n\n```ts\n// The MemoryAdapter contract, from `@tanstack/ai-memory`:\nimport type { MemoryAdapter } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\n```\n\nBuilt-in adapters, each a tree-shakeable subpath:\n\n```ts\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\nimport { redis } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/redis'\n```\n\nVendor adapters:\n\n```ts\nimport { hindsight } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/hindsight'\nimport { mem0 } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/mem0'\nimport { honcho } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/honcho'\n```\n\nSee [Adapters](./adapters) for every adapter and its options.\n\n## How a turn flows\n\n1. **Recall** runs before the model, during the run's `init` phase.\n   `adapter.recall(scope, userText)` returns memory, and the middleware adds the\n   `systemPrompt`, `toolGuidance`, and any `tools` to the run.\n2. **Save** runs after the stream finishes, deferred through `ctx.defer` so it never\n   blocks the response. The middleware hands the `{ user, assistant }` turn to\n   `adapter.save(scope, turn)`.\n\nTo add telemetry, watch memory in devtools, persist without recalling, or handle\nfailures, see [Operating memory](./operating).\n\n## Scope and security\n\n`MemoryScope` is the isolation boundary. It is an alias of the shared `Scope` identity\ntype from `@tanstack/ai` — the same vocabulary used by persistence — so memory and chat\ncenter on one conversation key:\n\n```ts\n// MemoryScope is an alias of Scope from `@tanstack/ai`, exported by `@tanstack/ai-memory`:\ntype MemoryScope = {\n  threadId: string // required — same as ChatMiddlewareContext.threadId\n  userId?: string\n  tenantId?: string\n  namespace?: string // reserved — no adapter keys on it yet\n}\n```\n\nAlways resolve scope on the server from trusted session/auth state. A client-originated\n`threadId` is fine only after you validate it belongs to the session user; never accept\n`userId`/`tenantId` from the request body alone. The function form of `scope` runs per\nrequest and only sees what your server attached to the chat context:\n\n```ts\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport type { MemoryAdapter } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\n\ndeclare const adapter: MemoryAdapter\ndeclare function getSession(ctx: unknown): { threadId: string; userId: string }\n\nmemoryMiddleware({\n  adapter,\n  scope: (ctx) => {\n    const session = getSession(ctx) // your server-validated session\n    return { threadId: session.threadId, userId: session.userId }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Next steps\n\n- [Quickstart](./quickstart): wire `memoryMiddleware` into a real `chat()` call\n- [Adapters](./adapters): every adapter's options, with an example of each\n- [Custom Adapter](./custom-adapter): implement `recall`/`save` for a backend that isn't shipped\n- [Operating memory](./operating): options, telemetry, devtools events, and failure behavior\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Overview\nid: memory-overview\norder: 1\ndescription: \"Give a TanStack AI chat() call memory across turns and sessions. memoryMiddleware recalls relevant memory into the prompt before the model runs, then saves each finished turn through a pluggable adapter.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - memory\n  - long-term memory\n  - retrieval\n  - persistence\n  - middleware\n  - rag\n  - personalization\n---\n\nYour assistant forgets everything the moment a session ends. A user tells it their name\nthis week; next week it asks again. `memoryMiddleware` fixes that. It gives a `chat()`\nrun memory that survives across turns and across sessions.\n\nIt works in two moves. Before the model runs, it **recalls** relevant memory from a\npluggable adapter and adds it to the system prompt. After the run finishes, it **saves**\nthe turn. The save is deferred, so it never blocks streaming.\n\nReach for it when you need recall across turns or sessions. To keep the last few messages\nof the same request, just pass them in `messages`. Memory is overkill for that.\n\nEverything lives in `@tanstack/ai-memory`: the middleware, the adapter contract, and the\nbuilt-in and vendor adapters.\n\n> Want a copy-paste setup? See the [Quickstart](./quickstart). Building an adapter for a\n> backend that isn't shipped? See the [Custom Adapter](./custom-adapter) guide.\n\n## When to reach for it\n\n| Need | Use this |\n|------|----------|\n| \"Remember what the user told me last week\" | Memory middleware with a persistent adapter |\n| \"Each user has their own context\" | Memory middleware with a scoped adapter |\n| \"Use a hosted memory service (mem0, Honcho, Hindsight)\" | The matching vendor adapter |\n| Keep the last few turns in the same request | Pass them in `messages`, skip memory |\n\n## The contract: recall and save\n\nA memory adapter has one identifier and two verbs. Extraction, ranking, rendering, and\nstorage are all the adapter's job. The middleware never looks inside a record.\n\n| Member | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `id` | Stable identifier used in logs and devtools. |\n| `recall(scope, query)` | Return what's relevant to `query` within `scope`: a rendered `systemPrompt`, optional `fragments`, and optional LLM `tools` plus `toolGuidance`. |\n| `save(scope, turn)` | Persist a finished `{ user, assistant }` turn. Extraction happens here. Returns one `SaveReceipt` per write. |\n| `inspect(scope)?` | Optional. A full snapshot for a devtools panel. |\n| `listFacts(scope)?` | Optional. A flat fact list for a devtools panel. |\n\n```ts\n// The MemoryAdapter contract, from `@tanstack/ai-memory`:\nimport type { MemoryAdapter } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\n```\n\nBuilt-in adapters, each a tree-shakeable subpath:\n\n```ts\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\nimport { redis } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/redis'\n```\n\nVendor adapters:\n\n```ts\nimport { hindsight } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/hindsight'\nimport { mem0 } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/mem0'\nimport { honcho } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/honcho'\n```\n\nSee [Adapters](./adapters) for every adapter and its options.\n\n## How a turn flows\n\n1. **Recall** runs before the model, during the run's `init` phase.\n   `adapter.recall(scope, userText)` returns memory, and the middleware adds the\n   `systemPrompt`, `toolGuidance`, and any `tools` to the run.\n2. **Save** runs after the stream finishes, deferred through `ctx.defer` so it never\n   blocks the response. The middleware hands the `{ user, assistant }` turn to\n   `adapter.save(scope, turn)`.\n\nTo add telemetry, watch memory in devtools, persist without recalling, or handle\nfailures, see [Operating memory](./operating).\n\n## Scope and security\n\n`MemoryScope` is the isolation boundary. It is an alias of the shared `Scope` identity\ntype from `@tanstack/ai` — the same vocabulary used by persistence — so memory and chat\ncenter on one conversation key:\n\n```ts\n// MemoryScope is an alias of Scope from `@tanstack/ai`, exported by `@tanstack/ai-memory`:\ntype MemoryScope = {\n  threadId: string // required — same as ChatMiddlewareContext.threadId\n  userId?: string\n  tenantId?: string\n  namespace?: string // reserved — no adapter keys on it yet\n}\n```\n\nAlways resolve scope on the server from trusted session/auth state. A client-originated\n`threadId` is fine only after you validate it belongs to the session user; never accept\n`userId`/`tenantId` from the request body alone. The function form of `scope` runs per\nrequest and only sees what your server attached to the chat context:\n\n```ts\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport type { MemoryAdapter } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\n\ndeclare const adapter: MemoryAdapter\ndeclare function getSession(ctx: unknown): { threadId: string; userId: string }\n\nmemoryMiddleware({\n  adapter,\n  scope: (ctx) => {\n    const session = getSession(ctx) // your server-validated session\n    return { threadId: session.threadId, userId: session.userId }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Next steps\n\n- [Quickstart](./quickstart): wire `memoryMiddleware` into a real `chat()` call\n- [Adapters](./adapters): every adapter's options, with an example of each\n- [Custom Adapter](./custom-adapter): implement `recall`/`save` for a backend that isn't shipped\n- [Operating memory](./operating): options, telemetry, devtools events, and failure behavior\n"}
